SUMMARY:[Artificial Life & Adaptive Systems][Computational Neuroscience] SA
 B 2026 - Poster abstract submission deadline (independent route)
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: International Conference on Simulation of Ada
 ptive Behavior\nWebsite: https://sab-conference.org/\nSource URL: https:/
 /sab-conference.org/call-for-contributions/\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany\n
 Topics: Artificial Life & Adaptive Systems\, Computational Neuroscience\,
  Cognitive Science & Computational Cognition\, Control & Robotics\nSize: 
 M\nSubmission type: Reviewed papers + non-archival contributions\nConfide
 nce: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-08\nNotes: Biennial ISAB confe
 rence. Reviewed track-1 papers appear in Springer LNAI\; the other tracks
  include non-archival papers\, poster abstracts and position papers. The 
 stated submission cutoff is Pacific Time\, not AoE\; May 15 uses daylight
  time. Size is an editorial estimate.\nScope: Understanding adaptive beha
 vior through biological and artificial agents\, including embodied cognit
 ion\, neural and computational models\, robotics\, learning\, evolution a
 nd collective behavior. The biennial ISAB meeting combines archival proce
 edings papers with deliberately non-archival contributions and poster abs
 tracts.\nAdditional topics: Machine Learning\, Reinforcement Learning\, A
 utonomous Agents & Multiagent Systems\nScope sources (2026): https://sab-
 conference.org/call-for-contributions/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-08
URL:https://sab-conference.org/call-for-contributions/
END:VEVENT
